# Core Rules

- App name is Yofai.
- Bundle ID is com.shawnwright.yofai.
- App type code word is Mosaic.
- Product purpose: local-first marketplace product photo preparation for online sellers.
- Core photo preparation is local-first/on-device.
- **Local Export Mode** is current production behavior: prepare/save/share local JPEGs; seller uploads manually.
- **Direct Upload Mode** is not implemented. It may be added later only after marketplace-specific official API/OAuth feasibility is verified and a phase is explicitly approved.
- Do not implement upload by guessing endpoints, browser automation, unofficial APIs, or storing marketplace passwords.
- Marketplaces are currently local export targets — do not claim live upload/publish exists.
- Marketplace destination (target) is separate from export pixel canvas; do not invent sizes for unverified markets.
- Export preset pixel sizes must not be invented; use verified sizes only.
- **Freemium-first if monetized:** Free keeps the core local export workflow from launch; Pro must be additive. Do not launch fully free and later lock existing core Free features behind payment.
- Do not delete seller data to enforce Free limits; over-limit existing products remain viewable/editable.
- Real StoreKit purchases are not implemented until an approved payments phase; do not fake purchase success.
- App Store launch claims must stay factual: local JPEG export for manual upload; no Direct Upload / compliance / partnership claims.
- Keep changes small.
- Inspect files before editing.
- Do not refactor unrelated files.
- Do not implement paid/live AI APIs unless explicitly re-approved. No AI API is required for export or future upload.
- Backend, accounts, cloud sync, subscriptions, and ads are future-capability only — not current work unless newly approved as a phase.
- Report changed files, build result, and next needed approval.
- Use short, simple explanations.
